{"repositoryId":1015724935,"availability":"available","full":"lars76/swift-f0","name":"swift-f0","description":"Fast and accurate fundamental frequency (F0) detector using convolutional neural networks","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":194,"forks":23,"created":"2025-07-08T00:23:13Z","updated":"2026-09-25T15:35:16Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["audio-analysis","convolutional-neural-networks","deep-learning","fundamental-frequency","machine-learning","onnx","pitch-detection","python","signal-processing","speech-processing"],"demo":"https://swift-f0.github.io/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:47.693Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:47.693Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:47.693Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T11:49:47.693Z","stars":194,"forks":23}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["SwiftF0 is a fast and accurate pitch detector for monophonic audio (one voice or instrument, not chords). A small neural network with 14 386 parameters reads the pitch from a spectrogram of the audio. For every frame it also gives a confidence that the pitch is right.","In the Pitch Detection Benchmark, SwiftF0 has the highest pitch F1 of the 19 trackers tested, statistically tied with RMVPE. It runs at 180 times real time on a single laptop CPU core. Streaming needs 176 ms of lookahead. It supports frequencies between 46.875 Hz and 2093.75 Hz (roughly F♯1 to C7). The article explains how it works and the training repository how it was trained."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lars76/swift-f0/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f23840b019a14281791ee1bbe8834dedb5bf9df9dfd7561f4659924f1ca7fb7c","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:47.748Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T11:49:47.748Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"SwiftF0 is a fast and accurate pitch detector for monophonic audio (one voice or instrument, not chords). A small